WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.120
Living systems have been around for a few 
billion years and will be around for many more.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:14.670
In the living world there's no landfill. Instead, 
materials flow. One species waste is another's  

3
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:22.470
food. Energy is provided by the Sun. Things grow 
then die and nutrients return to the soil safely.

4
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.720
And it works.

5
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.070
Yet, as humans, we've adopted a linear approach.

6
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:36.510
We take, we make, and we dispose. A new 
phone comes out, so we ditch the old one,

7
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.230
our washing machine packs up, so we buy another.

8
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.520
Each time we do this, we're 
eating into a finite supply  

9
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.910
of resources and often producing toxic waste.

10
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.610
It simply can't work long-term.

11
00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.460
So, what can?

12
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.980
If we accept that the living 
world's cyclical model works,  

13
00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:04.830
can we change our way of thinking, so 
that we to operate a circular economy?

14
00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:13.260
Let's start with the biological cycle. How can 
our waste build capital rather than reduce it?  

15
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:19.260
By rethinking and redesigning products and 
components and the packaging they come in,

16
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:25.080
we can create safe and compostable 
materials that help grow more stuff.

17
00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:31.170
As they say in the movies, no resources have 
been lost in the making of this material.

18
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.730
So, what about the washing 
machines, mobile phones, fridges?

19
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.590
We know they don't biodegrade.

20
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.820
Here, we're talking about another sort of rethink.

21
00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:47.970
A way to cycle valuable metals, polymers, 
and alloys so they maintain their quality

22
00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:53.010
and continue to be useful beyond the 
shelf life of individual products.

23
00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:58.170
What if the goods of today 
became the resources of tomorrow?

24
00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.300
It makes commercial sense.

25
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.650
Instead of the throw away and 
replace culture we become used to,

26
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.850
we'd adopt a return and renew one, where products  

27
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.810
and components are designed to 
be disassembled and regenerated.

28
00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:18.240
One solution may be to rethink 
the way we view ownership.

29
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:25.200
What if we never actually owned our technologies, 
we simply license them from the manufacturers?

30
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.800
Now let's put these two cycles together.

31
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:35.100
Imagine if we could design products to come 
back to their makers, their technical materials  

32
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:41.760
being reused, and their biological parts 
increasing agricultural value and imagine  

33
00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.060
that these products are made and transported 
using renewable energy. Here we have a model  

34
00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:53.880
that builds prosperity long-term, and the 
good news is there are already companies  

35
00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.920
out there who are beginning to adopt this 
way of working. But the circular economy  

36
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:05.610
isn't about one manufacturer changing one 
product. It's about all the interconnecting  

37
00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:11.820
companies that form our infrastructure and 
economy coming together. It's about energy,  

38
00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:20.820
it's about rethinking of the operating system 
itself. We have a fantastic opportunity to open  

39
00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:26.940
new perspectives and new horizons instead of 
remaining trapped in the frustrations of the  

40
00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:35.220
present with creativity and innovation, we 
really can rethink and redesign our future.
